I can see the vulnerability. In `dispatch`:
```c
pos1 = pos0 + 2;
offset = s->pc - pos1;
...
newpos = (int16_t)PEEK_S(s->iseq+pos0);
emit_S(s, pos0, (uint16_t)offset);
if (newpos == 0) return 0;
return pos1+newpos;
```

The `PEEK_S(s->iseq+pos0)` reads 2 bytes from `s->iseq+pos0`. If `pos0` points near the end of the buffer, this could read out of bounds. Let me look at `PEEK_S` and `emit_S`:

content:
